  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n**Model tier:** low\n\n## Context\n\nModel tier rationale: This replaces one unchecked test-fixture row access with an explicit guard and exercises that guard in the same integration file.\n\n- PR #1135, finding `27c2572469`, `backend/services/semprec-agents/src/__tests__/agentsTenantScope.test.ts:67`: runRow returns rows[0]! without proving that the query found the requested run.\n\n## Task\n\nReplace the non-null assertion in the local `runRow` helper with an explicit missing-row check that throws an Error naming the requested agent-run id. Preserve the helper's successful return shape. Add a focused same-file integration case requesting a valid but absent UUID and checking this diagnostic; retain the existing successful seeded-run checks.\n\n## Touches\n\n- backend/services/semprec-agents/src/__tests__/agentsTenantScope.test.ts (runRow and its missing-row regression only)\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\nThe runRow fixture boundary and its absent-row diagnostic.\n\n### Out of scope\n\nProduction agent-run lookup behavior, worker lifecycle and other non-null assertions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- For finding `27c2572469`, runRow rejects an absent UUID with an Error containing that UUID rather than returning undefined, and successful seeded-run queries retain their status/result values.\n\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=1135 key=27c2572469 -->",
